# 1. Rotating cube

The smallest program for a slide: a cube that turns by itself, in raw OpenGL 3.3 with GLFW, about 200
lines. The slide sets its speed and its tilt through the address of the frame; there is no control on
screen. One source builds for the desktop and for the web.

