## The files

```
examples/a1-opengl-cube/
  main.cpp           the program
  CMakeLists.txt     its build, desktop and web
  slides.html        the slide that shows it (reveal.js)
  web/               the web build: index.html (slide-frame.html), project.js, project.wasm
examples/cmake/raw_opengl_demo.cmake    the build of the raw OpenGL examples
examples/third_party/glad/              the OpenGL loader, for the desktop
bridge/                                 the bridge between the program and the slide
```

### main.cpp

One source for the desktop (OpenGL 3.3 core, GLFW, glad) and for the web (WebGL 2, which is OpenGL ES 3.0).
The four differences are marked with `#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__`:

1. **The headers:** `<GLES3/gl3.h>` on the web, glad on the desktop.
2. **The first line of the shaders:** `#version 300 es` and a `precision` on the web, `#version 330 core`
   on the desktop. The body of the shaders is the same; the program prepends the right line
   (`shader_header`).
3. **The size of the drawing:** the canvas of the page. The window is created at its size, otherwise
   `glfwCreateWindow` resizes the canvas, and the size is read at each frame (`surface_size`).
4. **The main loop:** on the web the browser calls `frame()` at each refresh (`emscripten_set_main_loop`).

The settings come from the command line, which the page of the demo builds from its address
(`?speed=0.2` gives `--speed 0.2`): three lines with the bridge, at the start of `main()`.

